st  uh new york customer uh with all the  black cars in new york kind of using our  tech to  do that pick up from the bank and take  you home at night um  product which was very popular you know  you back in the day a lot of  black cars were circling of the banks to  pick people up  yeah if you lived in new york you saw  down from any  major high price building class a office  space whether it was goldman sachs or  you know um a famous law firm or sherman  sterling or something there would just  be  tons and tons of lincoln town cars  circling to take people home for a  hundred bucks a pop to brooklyn  yeah that's exactly right and so we're  gonna be managing that for  for lehman brothers and enough like  literally we signed the contract to do  that about  two weeks before they went under um so  that really kind of messed the  new york plan up but we were gonna do  black cars in a much more aggressive way  in addition to taxis in new york in  particular  um but you know i think the really big  problem for us was the fact that  we never gave a product away for free um  like the the team at its core and in  particular our co-founder  um tom de pascuale who's a super amazing  uh businessman  but he had done a bunch of enterprise  businesses and so he really believed the  notion that hey you got to charge  um for everything right off the bat and  that was a mistake that we made we  should have gone freemium  offered the product for free gotten a  bunch of users and then  kind of so that throttled your growth  because people didn't even know you  existed and the only way they would know  you existed if they gave you money so  there's a huge lesson learned
 

